{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For I said, etc.</b> This is a reply to His saying ״מָה רָאִיתָ״, and he says <b>רַק</b> etc., because Avimelekh said to him: if you suspected them that they have no fear of Elohim, if so, would you not suspect that they would kill you and take your wife from you, and they would not be concerned about the prohibition of a married woman? Therefore he said ״רַק״ — an expression of diminution, to say that they do have some fear of Elohim, to lighten the severity of the matter through the fact that they would kill me. That is, for if they do not kill him, then for every single act of relations they would be liable to death and there would be a great punishment, and also all who come upon her would die. Therefore they would scheme to kill Avraham, and then there would be only the punishment of a single sin and a single person. And what is more, even if they kill him, if many people do it together there is a side of exemption. And therefore he was concerned and said ״my sister.״ And with this he also answered for not having informed him that she was his wife."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:31.822400185Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}